# pltfctl Compose inventory — the dev distro's Docker Compose stack. Compose
# distros only; shared settings live in infra/.infra.env, k3d ones in
# infra/k3d/fleet.env. Which Kafka runs is infra/compose/.variant.env.
#
# Read by scripts/pltfctl and scripts/projctl (sourced, after .infra.env).
# POSIX sh — plain KEY=value only, no expansion or substitution.

# --- dev ------------------------------------------------------------------
# One Kafka (infra/compose/dev-<variant>.yaml) and, in some variants, RustFS.
# Host ports bind 127.0.0.1 only. They avoid every k3d port in
# infra/k3d/fleet.env, but `up` still runs one distro at a time.
PLTF_DEV_PROJECT=pltf-dev          # docker compose -p: names containers, network, volumes
PLTF_DEV_KAFKA_PORT=9094           # host clients: localhost:9094 (PLAINTEXT)
PLTF_DEV_S3_PORT=9000              # RustFS S3 API:  http://localhost:9000
PLTF_DEV_S3_CONSOLE_PORT=9001      # RustFS console: http://localhost:9001
